{
  "schema": "omnibias/farm-ratios/v1",
  "supersedes": [
    "farm_time_to_target.json"
  ],
  "what": "Time to a relative-L2 target on the nine JAX problems of the registered end-to-end suite whose programs changed after it (Cahn-Hilliard, divergence-free flow, heat at D = 100 and 1,000, Helmholtz, HJB, log-determinant flow, Poisson at D = 100, tri-harmonic), re-run on a snapshot of the current code with the same protocol: the strongest omnibias pair against the strongest baseline pair, per target and per treatment of the compile time",
  "hardware": "one exclusive NVIDIA A100-SXM4-80GB, float64, three seeds per pair",
  "protocol": "ratio = baseline time / omnibias time, geometric mean over three seeds; lower = exp(mean log r - t(0.95, 2) sd / sqrt 3), upper = ratio^2 / lower; both pairs are the lowest-median pairs among those that reached the target in every seed, selected on the seeds that are compared (which favours the baseline when the choice is noisy); a target that no pair reached in every seed is incomplete, not a ratio",
